  "notes": "USAGE:\nOften used when discussing financial independence from parents or from government assistance. The concept is closely tied to the Japanese value of {自立|じりつ} (independence).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自活|じかつ}する (to support oneself)\n- {自活|じかつ}できる (to be able to support oneself)\n- {自活|じかつ}の{道|みち} (the path of self-support)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {自立|じりつ}: independence — broader concept including emotional and practical independence\n- {生計|せいけい}を{立|た}てる: to make a living — focuses on the act of earning a living",
